brow6el (A Chromium web browser for the terminal)
==================================================

brow6el is a full-featured web browser that runs inside your terminal.
It embeds Chromium through CEF (Chromium Embedded Framework) and renders
pages using the Sixel or Kitty terminal graphics protocol, with automatic
terminal detection. It offers vim-style modal navigation (standard,
insert, visual and mouse modes), hint mode, a JavaScript console,
bookmarks, user scripts, per-profile configuration, DNS-over-HTTPS and
proxy support.

Upstream:   https://codeberg.org/janantos/brow6el
Homepage:   https://www.brow6el.dev/
License:    MIT (uses CEF, BSD clause 3 exception; and libsixel, MIT)

This package is built from the pinned upstream commit (see brow6el.info:
COMMIT / VERSION). The binary self-reports version 0.3.4-45-gcd6be6e.

DEPENDENCIES
============
Build (already in Slackware -current core unless noted):
  cmake, g++ (C++20)
Requires from SlackBuilds.org (listed in REQUIRES):
  libsixel  (terminal Sixel graphics library, pkg-config: libsixel)

Runtime (pulled in by the bundled libcef.so; all Slackware core):
  glib, nspr, nss (+nssutil/smime), dbus, cups, libX11 and the X11/XCB
  stack (composite, damage, ext, fixes, randr, xcb), libgbm, expat,
  libxkbcommon, cairo, pango, libudev, alsa-lib, atk, at-spi2.

BUILD NOTES
===========
The build downloads the CEF (Chromium) binary distribution, a prebuilt
~309 MB tarball from cef-builds.spotifycdn.com (sha1 verified). This is
equivalent to vendoring a prebuilt dependency and is unavoidable; CEF is
not built from Chromium source here. The build then compiles the
libcef_dll_wrapper static library from that distribution and links
brow6el against it.

The CEF runtime (libcef.so plus the .pak resources, locales/, icudtl.dat,
v8_context_snapshot.bin, SwiftShader libs and the bundled .js scripts) is
installed next to the binary under /usr/lib/brow6el/ because the binary
finds libcef.so via RPATH=$ORIGIN. The /usr/bin/brow6el launcher sets
LD_LIBRARY_PATH and the Vulkan ICD (vk_swiftshader_icd.json) before
exec'ing the real binary, mirroring the upstream run_brow6el.sh.

NOTE: the package ships with RPATH=/RUNPATH=$ORIGIN on both the binary and
libcef.so, so they resolve to the co-located files under /usr/lib/brow6el
rather than any system library of the same name. If a linter flags the
rpath, this is expected and correct here.

brow6el runs Chromium with --no-sandbox (settings.no_sandbox = true), so
no setuid chrome-sandbox helper is required.

BUILDING
========
  source ./brow6el.info
  wget -O brow6el-cd6be6e.tar.gz "$DOWNLOAD"
  md5sum -c <(echo "$MD5SUM  brow6el-cd6be6e.tar.gz")
  ./brow6el.SlackBuild

The CEF download happens automatically during the build.

RUNNING
=======
  brow6el https://example.com
  brow6el --help

On first run a default Chromium flag config is written to
~/.brow6el/cef_flags.conf. Press the "I" (insert) / "S" (standard) /
"V" (visual) / "M" (mouse) keys to switch modes; see the README.md in
/usr/doc/brow6el-<version>/ for the full key reference.

KNOWN ISSUES
============
Kitty graphics over SSH is slow (large base64 transfers per frame); Sixel
is the recommended protocol, especially over SSH. Requires a terminal
with Sixel (foot, WezTerm, kitty, Ghostty, ...) or Kitty support.
